# search: tools/searchcheck.py's session (not a DOS golden: it has a test's cheat, format 6),
# recorded by the port from this script from the saved game setup/plain-debris writes (a new
# character on level 1). "Journey Onward" and the first saved game; then the test's cheat goto
# 1 43 9, a teleport within the level onto (43,9), a diagonal tile open to the south east, whose
# wall runs through the middle of the square, so the player does not fit there. do_teleport's
# find_good_x_and_y then tries the two squares the diagonal opens onto: (44,9), east, open
# floor, where the player fits, and (43,8), rock. (44,9) is in the column after the start's,
# whose bits in the visited table the original never clears; the port left them to its own
# stack and refused the teleport ("no free square there"); with the whole table cleared the
# player lands on (44,9)
3000 key enter         # Journey Onward
4500 key enter         # the first saved game
8000 cheat goto 1 43 9
